-- title:
--   Stalk dictionary for the chart algebras of `TwoChartIntegralModel`
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`.
--
--   **Arithmetic frame.** Fixed are a prime $q$ with $5 \le q$, a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; write $k =$ `ResidueField A`. Two function fields occur: `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((t))$ generated over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ by the image under coefficientwise extension `coeffEmb` of `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`, and `fieldBar q M'` $=$ `xHFunctionFieldBar (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`, the analogous base change of the $X_H$ function field of level $q^2M'$ for the subgroup `levelH q M'`, which is the kernel of the reduction map $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. A finset $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC k M'` over $k$ is given together with the hypothesis `hW`, which says that $W$ consists exactly of the members of `ssPlaces q M' k`: the places $w$ that are rational, satisfy `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and have $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{jGeomGen}\,k\,M') \in$ `ssJSet q k`, the set of those $j \in k$ such that every elliptic curve over $k$ with invariant $j$ has no nonzero $k$-point killed by $q$. Further given are `hle`, the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` $\le$ `fieldBar q M'`, a `ConstantReduction` $R_0$ of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC k M'` (a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, a surjective residue map onto `modularFunctionFieldC k M'` with kernel the maximal ideal, a map on places preserving degrees, and the compatibility axioms of that structure), and `hR₀`, which requires that for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((t))$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue is, as a Laurent series over $k$, the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   **Igusa and supersingular valuation rings.** Fixed are an index $\zeta$ in `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$), a family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of valuation subrings of `fieldBar q M'` indexed by [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21) $= \mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$, and a family $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ of valuation subrings of `fieldBar q M'` indexed by $W$, subject to the following hypotheses. `hIg_inf`: $f \in O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ holds precisely when $f = x/y$ for Laurent series $x,y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise reduction of $y$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ is nonzero. `hIg`: every $\ell \in \mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ is $\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma \cdot \mathrm{lineInfty}\,q$ for some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ for which $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ is the pullback of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`. `hIg_inj`: $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ is injective. `hIg_perm`: for every index $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ the pullbacks of the $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` permute the family. `hSS_A`: for each $s \in W$ and $x \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$, the image of $x$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ iff $x \in A$. `hSS_over`: for $s \in W$ and $f \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ such that $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(f)$ at every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which the Laurent expansion of `jq` is regular, and such that the $R_0$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$, and for every $a \in A$ whose residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that $R_0$-residue, the difference of the image of $f$ and the image of $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$. `hSS_fix`: each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is stable under pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for all $\zeta'$ and all $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$. `hSS_tr`: each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ contains an element $t$ such that $t$ minus the image of any $a \in A$ is a unit of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$. Finally a `RegularProlongation` $R$ of $A$ from `fieldBar q M'` to `xHFunctionFieldC k (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')` is given with `hR`: $R.\mathrm{integers} = O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$, together with `hR₀O`: membership of $f$ in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ is equivalent to membership of its image in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$.
--
--   **Base-field data.** Given are $\pi \in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$; an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$ such that $A \cap k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is Henselian, and has algebraically closed residue field; `hκ`: every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$. Given further are a prime $\ell$ with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \ne q$, $\ell \nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity; and $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. Finally, $K_1$ is a finite extension of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $A_1$ a valuation subring of $K_1$ consisting exactly of the elements of $K_1$ lying in $A$, assumed to be a Henselian discrete valuation ring.
--
--   **The geometric frame.** The field `fieldBar q M'` carries the $k_0$-algebra structure obtained by composing $k_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\overline{\mathbb Q} \to$ `fieldBar q M'`. The assertion is then universally quantified over an intermediate field $F_0$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ satisfying four conditions: the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is all of `fieldBar q M'`; $F_0$ is stable under every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, every family $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and every family $a$ of elements of the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, a relation $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ forces all $a_i = 0$; and every element of `fieldBar q M'` whose Laurent series has coefficients in the image of $\mathbb Q$ lies in $F_0$.
--
--   Write $L_1$ for the compositum, inside `fieldBar q M'`, of $F_0$ and the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_1$. The assertion is further quantified over an $A_1$-algebra structure on $L_1$ whose structure map sends each $a \in A_1$ to the image of $a$ under $\overline{\mathbb Q} \to$ `fieldBar q M'`, and over an element $j_1 \in L_1$ whose image in `fieldBar q M'` is the inclusion of the Laurent expansion `jq` of the $j$-function, with $j_1 \ne 0$.
--
--   Let $\mathfrak X =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A₁ L₁ j₁`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout of the two morphisms `fFin`, `fInf` out of the middle chart; its two charts are $X_{\mathrm{fin}} = \operatorname{Spec}$ of `chartAlgFin`, the subalgebra of elements of $L_1$ integral over $A_1[j_1]$, and $X_\infty = \operatorname{Spec}$ of `chartAlgInf`, the elements integral over $A_1[j_1^{-1}]$, with canonical morphisms `ιFin`, `ιInf` into $\mathfrak X$.
--
--   Four predicates are introduced in the statement. For a point $x$ of $\mathfrak X$ and $f \in L_1$, `InStalk x f` says: for every prime $y$ of `chartAlgFin` with `ιFin.base y = x` there are $g,h \in$ `chartAlgFin` with $h \notin y$ and $f h = g$ in $L_1$, and likewise for every prime $y$ of `chartAlgInf` with `ιInf.base y = x` with $g,h \in$ `chartAlgInf`. `InMax x f` is the same statement with the extra requirement $g \in y$ in both clauses. `Centred P x`, for $P$ a place of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, says that $P$ is rational and that every $f \in L_1$ with `InStalk x f` lies in the valuation subring of $P$, has $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) \in A$, and satisfies: the $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ is $< 1$ if and only if `InMax x f`. `GoodPt x` says that `toBase.base x` is the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$, that every $y$ with $x \rightsquigarrow y$ equals $x$, that for every prime $y$ of either chart lying over $x$ every chart element whose image in `fieldBar q M'` is a non-unit of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ lies in $y$, and that for every prime $y$ of `chartAlgFin` over $x$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi :$ `chartAlgFin` $\to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(\mathrm{jChartFin})$ does not lie in `ssJSet q Ω`. The predicates `Centred` and `GoodPt` are part of this frame and do not occur in the conclusion.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Two conjuncts.
--
--   First: for every prime $y$ of `chartAlgFin` and every $b \in$ `chartAlgFin`, writing $x =$ `ιFin.base y`, the element $b$ of $L_1$ satisfies `InStalk x b`, and `InMax x b` holds if and only if $b \in y$.
--
--   Second: for every prime $y$ of `chartAlgInf` and every $b \in$ `chartAlgInf`, writing $x =$ `ιInf.base y`, the element $b$ of $L_1$ satisfies `InStalk x b`, and `InMax x b` holds if and only if $b \in y$.
--
--   This is the chart-side half of the stalk dictionary for the two-chart integral model of the level field over the Henselian discrete valuation ring $A_1$: an element of either chart algebra is regular at every point of the pushout above its own prime, read in either chart, and it is a non-unit in the local ring exactly when it belongs to that prime. It is used by the results that produce a point of the model centred at a place, that analyse the $j$-invariant of the chart at such a point, and that extract an étale coordinate in residue characteristic $q$.
